From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:05:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] autostart: Skip X11-only entries under Caminito

Under Caminito, the Wayland compositor for MATE, mate-session unsets
GDK_BACKEND, so what it starts opens GDK on Wayland. mate-screensaver and
mate-maximus call Xlib without checking for an X display, and die with
SIGSEGV at every login. plank, Ubuntu MATE's dock, calls GDK's X11
functions unchecked too.

None of these has work to do there, and on XWayland each would see the
XWayland windows alone:

- Caminito owns org.mate.ScreenSaver before mate-session starts, so
  mate-screensaver would find the name taken and exit.
- mate-maximus takes the decorations off maximised windows through X11,
  which is the compositor's decision under Caminito.
- mate-hud searches the focused window's menu, found through X11's active
  window. Under Caminito, Caminito brokers the menus.
- plank is a dock, through libwnck. mate-panel's tasklist lists the windows
  under Caminito. It starts as the dock required component, and Ubuntu
  MATE's dock-replace starts it again.
- picom is an X compositor, and magnus a magnifier that reads the X root
  window. Both are the compositor's work.

Treat their autostart entries as disabled when MATE_WM_NAME is Caminito,
whichever autostart directory they are read from. Without that variable,
nothing changes.
---
 mate-session/gsm-autostart-app.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mate-session/gsm-autostart-app.c b/mate-session/gsm-autostart-app.c
index a23a132..b441a4c 100644
--- a/mate-session/gsm-autostart-app.c
+++ b/mate-session/gsm-autostart-app.c
@@ -108,6 +108,27 @@ gsm_autostart_app_init (GsmAutostartApp *app)
         priv->autostart_delay = -1;
 }
 
+/* Autostart entries that must not start under Caminito, the Wayland compositor
+ * for MATE. Each is X11-only, and its work is Caminito's or the compositor's, so
+ * on XWayland it would see the XWayland windows alone. plank is the dock
+ * required component, and dock-replace starts it again. */
+static const char * const caminito_skipped_ids[] = {
+        "mate-screensaver.desktop",       /* Caminito owns org.mate.ScreenSaver */
+        "mate-maximus-autostart.desktop", /* undecorates maximised windows */
+        "mate-hud.desktop",               /* searches the focused window's menu */
+        "plank.desktop",                  /* a dock: mate-panel's tasklist */
+        "dock-replace.desktop",
+        "picom.desktop",                  /* an X compositor */
+        "magnus-autostart.desktop",       /* a magnifier */
+        NULL
+};
+
+static gboolean
+is_under_caminito (void)
+{
+        return g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Caminito") == 0;
+}
+
 static gboolean
 is_disabled (GsmApp *app)
 {
@@ -115,6 +136,13 @@ is_disabled (GsmApp *app)
 
         priv = gsm_autostart_app_get_instance_private (GSM_AUTOSTART_APP(app));
 
+        if (is_under_caminito () && priv->desktop_id != NULL &&
+            g_strv_contains (caminito_skipped_ids, priv->desktop_id)) {
+                g_debug ("app %s is disabled under Caminito",
+                         gsm_app_peek_id (app));
+                return TRUE;
+        }
+
         /* Hidden key, used by autostart spec */
         if (egg_desktop_file_get_boolean (priv->desktop_file,
                                           EGG_DESKTOP_FILE_KEY_HIDDEN, NULL)) {
